cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  truffle: Create datasets with known effects hidden in messy data for teaching
  data wrangling
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite it as below.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Hussey
    given-names: Ian
    email: ian.hussey@unibe.ch
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-8906-7559"
abstract: >-
  Generate datasets with known statistical effects (truffles) that students must
  rediscover, then bury them in realistic data-processing challenges (dirt) that
  must be cleaned first. Generated data contain demographics and item-level
  Likert responses, with known differences in sum-score means between
  conditions, known correlations between outcomes, and known Cronbach's alpha
  per scale. Data can be made messy in many ways to create realistic wrangling
  exercises for teaching.
keywords:
  - teaching
  - data wrangling
  - simulated data
  - statistics education
  - R
